 "answer": {
  "answer": "The goal was not met. The code confirmed 2 of the 5 cases it was looking for (S12 and S22), and only one of those two is a failure of the policy. On scene 09a95ffa, shifting the cars 1.5 s earlier at recorded speed (S12) made every run fail the same way: the ego moved left into car 33, which the retiming had placed alongside it. That collision is real and the policy caused it, but with only a few repeats we can say its failure rate is above one half, not how high it is. The other confirmed case, scene 0e899dd3 at 0 s shift and 0.5x speed (S22), and the two failures on 023b7fcc (S2) all happened before or at the moment the policy took control. They come from the retimed or reconstructed traffic, not from the policy. The other six scenes did not fail at any setting tried, though most settings got only one run.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "On scene 09a95ffa, shifting the cars 1.5 s earlier at recorded speed makes the policy collide, and the code confirmed this case. In every run the ego steered left into car 33, which was coming up alongside in the left lane, and hit it with its front-left corner. The lead car was far ahead, so this was not a following-distance failure. The triage blames the policy every time.",
    "settings": [
     "S12"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On the same scene with the same 1.5 s earlier shift at 2x speed, the single run also failed, but in a different way: the ego stayed one lane left of the recorded path, ignored the RIGHT command, and ran into slower car 87 ahead without braking enough. This is one run, so it is a hint, not a rate. It is also flagged as a possible simulator artifact because the ego was more than 3.5 m off the recording.",
    "settings": [
     "S13"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On scene 09a95ffa the failures depend on speed: at 0.75x speed, neither the 1.5 s nor the 2 s earlier shift produced a failure. The danger seems to need the shifted cars at recorded speed or faster.",
    "settings": [
     "S10",
     "S11",
     "S12",
     "S13"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "The confirmed case on scene 0e899dd3 (0 s shift, 0.5x speed) is not the policy's fault. In every run the ego was still replaying the human drive while it closed on the slowed pickup ahead, and the front collision was recorded at the handoff frame. The policy never had control before the crash. The cause is the slowed lead car, which replay could not react to.",
    "settings": [
     "S22"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "The failures on scene 023b7fcc (0.5 s later, 0.5x speed) are also not the policy's fault. Actor 12 overlaps the ego about two seconds before the policy takes over and appears as a smeared car on the hood, which points to a bad reconstructed track. The same scene with recorded timing did not fail.",
    "settings": [
     "S2",
     "S1"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "Three settings that got enough repeats look safe: their failure rate is confidently below one half, and no run failed. These are 12855a41 at 2 s earlier and 0.75x, 19f339ba at 0.5 s later and 1.5x, and 1c45ce3a at 1 s later and 0.75x.",
    "settings": [
     "S23",
     "S29",
     "S33"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "No failure was found on scenes 054b5901, 0cf6368d, 12855a41, 19f339ba or 1c45ce3a, or on 0e899dd3 outside the 0.5x setting. That includes the full range of shifts and speeds for the cut-in car singled out on 0cf6368d, 12855a41 and 1c45ce3a. Most of these settings got a single run, so they are not shown to be safe.",
